DATA SOURCES
    This project distributes no bank data. The repository, the released
    binaries and the container image contain parsers only. "iban-pizza update"
    downloads each registry from its official publisher onto the machine of
    whoever runs it, and the terms of that publisher apply to that person and
    to the data they downloaded. "iban-pizza sources" prints, for every
    registry, the publisher, where its terms are published and the source
    statement it asks for; the same is stored with the data and reported by
    the service at /v2/data.

    The terms differ. Some registries are under an open licence (CC BY 4.0 for
    Austria, Italy and Slovenia). Most are under the publisher's own terms of
    use, which typically allow use and reproduction with the source named and
    in several cases forbid passing the data on altered. A few state no terms
    at all. Anyone who intends to pass downloaded data on to others, rather
    than use it to run the service, has to check the terms of each registry
    for that purpose.

    Where a registry names an institution's LEI but no BIC, the BIC is joined
    from the BIC-to-LEI mapping table published by SWIFT and GLEIF. That table
    is not covered by GLEIF's CC0 dedication; it is licensed under the BIC/LEI
    Mapping Table License Agreement, which permits any use provided this
    notice accompanies copies of the table, in whole or in part:

        SWIFT (c) and database rights. All rights reserved. This Mapping Table
        has been developed by SWIFT. Any use of the Mapping Table, in whole or
        in part, is subject to the BIC/LEI Mapping Table License Agreement as
        published with the Mapping Table available on GLEIF's website. The
        Mapping Table is updated monthly. For the latest BIC information and
        updates, always refer to www.swift.com/bic.

    The test fixtures under internal/sources/testdata and
    cmd/iban-pizza/testdata hold a handful of rows in each registry's layout
    for the parsers' tests. They are not a dataset and are not used at run
    time.
